> f(x: u8) = x / x
> g(x: u8) = 1
> domain f
domain of f:
  x: u8, 0..255
  requires x != 0  (in x/x)
  defined at 255 of 256 points
  defined for: 1..255
  undefined e.g. at x=0
  C undefined behaviour at 1 points, e.g. x=0
  over all 256 points of the domain
> domain g
domain of g:
  x: u8, 0..255
  defined at 256 of 256 points
  no conditions: total on its parameter types
  over all 256 points of the domain
> equiv f g
f and g are equal on the domain of f (exhaustive)
> equiv g f
g and f differ at 1 point, e.g. x=0: 1 vs undefined
